.DS_Store
node_modules
/build
/.svelte-kit
/package

# Cargo build output. Now at the workspace root rather than under src-tauri/,
# because a workspace shares one target directory across all members.
/target
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# Python bytecode, from scripts/ (the dash ratchet and its tests)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The OCR model files, their verified upstream downloads, and the generated
# NOTICE. Written by TWO scripts, which is the part that used to be wrong here:
# scripts/convert-ppocr-models.py converts the recogniser and the dictionary,
# and scripts/acquire-ppocr-detector.py DOWNLOADS the detector already in ONNX
# from Baidu (ADR-0036). Saying "converted ... by convert-ppocr-models.py" told
# a reader the wrong provenance for one of the three.
#
# NEVER committed. ADR-0034 decided we convert the official release ourselves,
# and ADR-0004 keeps this repository public and GPL-3.0: ~21 MB of third-party
# model weights do not belong in its history, where they would be permanent.
# The manifest in crates/uptake-assets/src/ppocr.rs carries their digests, which
# is the part that IS ours to version.
/dist

# The staging directory the installer packages: the ONNX Runtime DLL, its two
# notice files, and the OCR models. ~37 MB of binaries that are ACQUIRED rather
# than committed -- `scripts/acquire-onnxruntime.py`,
# `scripts/acquire-ppocr-detector.py` and `scripts/convert-ppocr-models.py`
# each verify every byte against a pinned SHA-256 before writing here, which is
# ADR-0032 decision 2.
#
# ⚠️ This block said "the converted PP-OCRv4 models", named TWO scripts, and
# said ~31 MB. All three were stale, and it sits eleven lines below the block
# this pull request edited specifically to correct the same provenance claim --
# PR #88 round 10, FINDING 2. The detector is Baidu's own ONNX and is not
# converted here (ADR-0036). Committing them
# would put unreviewable binaries in a public repository and make the pin a
# description rather than a check.
/src-tauri/assets
